From fe08b588e7c65a0621bb74839d1d18b3d1bb3949 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:38:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 172/177] box: outbounds replaced while the box runs

UpdateOutbounds builds the given outbounds, each in a scope of its own,
starts them after their dependencies among them and puts them in the
manager under their tags; the router, the Clash API and the reference
manager find outbounds by tag, so new connections go through them while
open ones keep the objects of their chains. An outbound that stays may
not depend on one that changes. A failure puts the outbounds of before
back and closes the new ones.

A urltest group that is replaced stops testing, choosing and judging;
the group taking its tag keeps its choice when it has the same member
and tests only the members without a result, three at a time. The
groups count the connections they dialed by member.

What was replaced or taken out is kept while a connection in the list
of the Clash API goes through it, or a kept group dialed one through it,
at least two minutes and at most a day; groups let go of their members
after two minutes. Beyond a limit of kept servers the update is refused
and the caller makes a new box.

The block outbound is back in podkop_slim: a section whose group has no
server refuses its connections through a selector of it.
